A heap is a "tree-based" data structure that satisfies the heap property. 
It keeps itself organized so you can always wquickly grab the smallest (or largest) element

A heap is just a "binary tree" which follows the heap property. There are two heap properties for the 2 "flavors" of heap
    "min-heap": every parent node is smaller than ( or equal to) its children.
    "max-heap": every parent node is larger than (or equal to) its children.

    and it also has the shape property  - it must be a complete b inary tree.

you have to learn what a binary tree is










